"poster\":\"4c964c3aafaa003796e8619a07814f0d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Dress to sweat\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2460814\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"club\"}],\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"artists\":[{\"id\":2056,\"artist_name\":\"Scott Fraser\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2057,\"artist_name\":\"Joe Hart\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"venues\":[{\"id\":3,\"name\":\"Spanners\",\"address\":\"Arch 504, Ridgway Rd\",\"city\":\"London\",\"country\":\"U.K.\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"promoters\":[{\"id\":381,\"name\":\"Body Hammer\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"stripe_account_id\":\"\",\"ticket_email\":\"\",\"custom_domain\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"tags\":[{\"id\":9,\"name\":\"house\"},{\"id\":24,\"name\":\"electro\"}]},{\"id\":860,\"name\":\"ORMSIDE presents: Nkisi\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-15T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-16T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"66198cb4e190992231b108ac9578b539.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"On Saturday 15th August, Ormside welcomes back a true pillar of our sonic identity. Nkisi returns for a defining, all-night-long session after nearly a decade of shared history within the space.\\n\\nInviting us into her expansive ethnographic research practice and distinctive sound world, she offers total immersion via rhythmic cycles and ceremonial sonics. Across the night, she will guide the room through five distinct chapters – a deliberate, unfolding procession exploring temporality, repetition, and trance-states\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2492439\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"club\"}],\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"artists\":[{\"id\":116,\"artist_name\":\"Nkisi\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"venues\":[{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"Ormside Projects\",\"address\":\"Penarth Centre, 32 Ormside Street\",\"city\":\"London\",\"country\":\"U.K.\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"promoters\":[{\"id\":53,\"name\":\"Ormside Projects\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"stripe_account_id\":\"\",\"ticket_email\":\"\",\"custom_domain\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"ticket_tiers\":[{\"id\":779,\"name\":\"2nd Release\",\"price\":12.45,\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"quantity_available\":15,\"quantity_sold\":1,\"resale_listed_count\":0,\"hidden\":false,\"password_protected\":false,\"is_pwyc\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"resale_enabled\":true,\"resale_when_event_sold_out\":false,\"sort_order\":0,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":780,\"name\":\"Entry Before Midnight\",\"price\":9.43,\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"quantity_available\":10,\"quantity_sold\":6,\"resale_listed_count\":0,\"hidden\":false,\"password_protected\":false,\"is_pwyc\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"resale_enabled\":true,\"resale_when_event_sold_out\":true,\"sort_order\":0,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}]},{\"id\":165,\"name\":\"Zu\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-18T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-18T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"228a2b635d9a2d439c1d5da20ca39b90.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\n\\nZu\\nAn Italian jazz-punk-noise explosion, and you can dance to it. Shook the building to it's core last summer and back to do it all again, armed with a new album. \\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\n£17\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/zu-1\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"gig\"}],\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"artists\":[{\"id\":477,\"artist_name\":\"Zu\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"venues\":[{\"id\":65,\"name\":\"New Cross Inn\",\"address\":\"323 New Cross Road\",\"city\":\"London\",\"country\":\"\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"promoters\":[{\"id\":94,\"name\":\"Real Life Presents\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"stripe_account_id\":\"\",\"ticket_email\":\"\",\"custom_domain\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"tags\":[{\"id\":23,\"name\":\"jazz\"},{\"id\":37,\"name\":\"noise\"},{\"id\":38,\"name\":\"dark-jazz\"}]},{\"id\":886,\"name\":\"LITF Presents: STRANGE(R) PAGES\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-18T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-18T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"91313ab96a3a422e1aa77003daf57523.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Lost in the Foxglove: Regular Poetry Club would love to welcome you to a brand new series fixture at Rhizomatic!. This time you're invited to STRANGE(R) PAGES. A combination poetry workshop, open mic event where guests are equipped with the tools to begin a brand new poem, and perform on the mic on the same night. Though, the twist is you won't be reading your own work aloud. \\n\\nThis event is perfect for anyone whose been wanting to work up the courage to perform, but has been too nervous to take the leap. You might be wondering what I could possibly mean by this… Seems like you'll just have to come and find out. Think queer, community, low-pressure, creativity, and play. \\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/37162/litf-presents-stranger-pages\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":8,\"name\":\"poetry\"}],\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"venues\":[{\"id\":241,\"name\":\"Rhizomatic\",\"address\":\"\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"promoters\":[{\"id\":402,\"name\":\"Lost in the Foxglove\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"stripe_account_id\":\"\",\"ticket_email\":\"\",\"custom_domain\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"tags\":[{\"id\":191,\"name\":\"Queer\"},{\"id\":211,\"name\":\"poetry\"},{\"id\":212,\"name\":\"open mic\"},{\"id\":622,\"name\":\"FLINTA\"}]},{\"id\":887,\"name\":\"‘Flamboyance’ with Jack Parlett in conversation with Peter Scalpello\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-18T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-18T20:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"99cd1b97b12c6ed4e81c9a3dce715f4b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"JACK PARLETT AND CELEBRATED POET PETER SCALPELLO DISCUSS ‘FLAMBOYANCE’ AND HOW IT IGNITES EVERY ASPECT OF OUR LIVES, FROM ART AND ENTERTAINMENT TO RITUAL AND PROTEST.\\nFlamboyance is Jack Parlett’s follow up to his acclaimed Fire Island (A Housmans bestseller of 2022). This new book has all the qualities one has come to expect of Jack’s work; big hearted and erudite in equal measure.\\n\\nFlamboyance ignites every aspect of our lives, from art and entertainment to ritual and protest. The word conjures exuberance and unashamed passion; in thought, expression and dress. Yet historically the term ‘flamboyant’ has been reserved for the over-the-top and the outré, invoked at times as a pejorative innuendo or worse.\\n\\nIn his fascinating new book, Jack Parlett argues for its value as an empowering and creative force, illuminating the ways in which flamboyance is a fundamental aspect of human conduct that both marks and transcends difference.\\n\\nTaking in an eclectic array of examples, from Gothic architecture to the orange flowers of Dungeness, and populated by figures such as Oscar Wilde, James Baldwin, Elton John, Amy Winehouse, Lil Nas X and Chappell Roan, this is a book about flamboyant art and the art of flamboyance. And having both aspired to it and rejected it, Jack recounts his personal relationship to flamboyance while also finding new meanings of the word, exploring its surprises and contradictions, and reconnecting with its radical power.\\n\\nOUR SPEAKERS:\\n\\nJack Parlett is the author of three books: The Poetics of Cruising: Queer Visual Culture from Whitman to Grindr (a monograph with University of Minnesota Press), Same Blue, Different You (a poetry pamphlet with Broken Sleep Books), and Fire Island: A Queer History (Granta), which was named one of the Best Books of 2022 by the New Yorker and shortlisted for the Polari Book Prize 2023. His writing has appeared in the New Yorker, Document Journal, BBC Culture, Boston Review, Literary Hub and Poetry London.\\n\\nPeter Scalpello is a writer and psychotherapist from Glasgow, based in London. Their second book, Mirrorstage, was published this year with Cipher Press.\\n\\nAs always, tickets are priced on a sliding scale. If you are unable to pay for a ticket please do not hesitate to contact us at shop@housmans.com, and a free ticket will be made available.\\n\\nIf you choose ‘book + entry’ your copies of the book will be available to collect on the evening. If you would like to collect it earlier, or arrange for delivery, please contact us (postage is £2.95). Telephone 020 7837 4473 or email shop@housmans.com.\\n\\nDoors Open at 6:45pm, Event Starts 7:00.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://housmans.com/event/book-launch-flamboyance-with-jack-parlett/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":10,\"name\":\"talk\"}],\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"artists\":[{\"id\":1128,\"artist_name\":\"Jack Parlett\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2287,\"artist_name\":\"Peter Scalpello\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"venues\":[{\"id\":76,\"name\":\"Housmans Bookshop\",\"address\":\"5 Caledonian Road\",\"city\":\"London\",\"country\":\"\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}]},{\"id\":888,\"name\":\"HOUSMANS READING SERIES: Robert Glück\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-19T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-19T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a2ec0f59913a5b1ce4cfeb0f3f62e732.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Housmans are beyond honoured, and slightly delightedly flabbergasted, to welcome the legendary writer Robert Glück to the shop for a reading. Robert, or Bob, is one of the most important writers working in the world today, in a career that spans many decades, poetry and cutting edge fiction; his work has been of profound importance to the contemporary queer literary landscape.\\n\\nReading alongside Bob we’ve some of the most exciting younger writers working in London today: Oisín Roberts, JD Howse and Luke Roberts.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://housmans.com/event/housmans-reading-series-robert-gluck/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":10,\"name\":\"talk\"}],\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"artists\":[{\"id\":1935,\"artist_name\":\"JD Howse\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2161,\"artist_name\":\"Oisín Roberts\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2288,\"artist_name\":\"Robert Glück\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2289,\"artist_name\":\"Luke Roberts\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"venues\":[{\"id\":76,\"name\":\"Housmans Bookshop\",\"address\":\"5 Caledonian Road\",\"city\":\"London\",\"country\":\"\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"tags\":[{\"id\":211,\"name\":\"poetry\"},{\"id\":477,\"name\":\"queer fiction\"}]},{\"id\":832,\"name\":\"Deptford Junction Presents: Tasska, Psychoma, Speed Trials\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-19T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-19T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5c99c1683354923e5afca9f20c8709e6.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Tasska - Targeting the social fractures emerging from a country on the brink, Tasska are a band emboldened by vulnerability and honesty. Drawing from the lyrical wryness of artists like Orange Juice and Jonathan Richman, and the bite of bands like Cola and Television, Tasska have forged the gut-punch and grace of their live performance in front of hometown Brighton audience. They're on the up, and not to be missed...\\n\\nPsychoma - A singular, unified vision: to resurrect the raw power of the grunge era and inject it with the modern intensity of hardcore and shoegaze. They aren't just playing alt-rock; they are building a wall of sound designed to envelop, disorient, and completely captivate the London underground.\\n\\nSpeed Trials - Speed Trials is a London based groovy grunge band. Within every dark cloud is a silver lining - they have arrived to part them all.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":false,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"gig\"}],\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"artists\":[{\"id\":2137,\"artist_name\":\"Tasska\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2138,\"artist_name\":\"Psychoma\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2139,\"artist_name\":\"Speed Trials\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"venues\":[{\"id\":140,\"name\":\"Deptford Junction\",\"address\":\"Unit 8, Titan Business Estate, Ffinch St\",\"city\":\"London\",\"country\":\"\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"promoters\":[{\"id\":221,\"name\":\"Deptford Junction\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"stripe_account_id\":\"\",\"ticket_email\":\"\",\"custom_domain\":\"\",\"on_listings_si