laying the early groundwork for modern trap and phonk.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2469486\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"club\"},{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"gig\"}],\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"artists\":[{\"id\":1118,\"artist_name\":\"Nihal El Aasar\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":1642,\"artist_name\":\"James Massiah\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":1958,\"artist_name\":\"DJ Spanish Fly\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"venues\":[{\"id\":84,\"name\":\"Venue MOT\",\"address\":\"Orion Business Centre, Surrey Canal Rd\",\"city\":\"London\",\"country\":\"\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"promoters\":[{\"id\":368,\"name\":\"VENT\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"stripe_account_id\":\"\",\"ticket_email\":\"\",\"custom_domain\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"tags\":[{\"id\":86,\"name\":\"hiphop\"},{\"id\":503,\"name\":\"rap\"},{\"id\":539,\"name\":\"memphis\"},{\"id\":540,\"name\":\"trap\"}]},{\"id\":844,\"name\":\"Form Affinity | Gil Shani Trio\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-21T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-21T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"09a0dd499e912f4a78ec81028d9afb9a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"gig\"}],\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"artists\":[{\"id\":1175,\"artist_name\":\"Form Affinity\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2166,\"artist_name\":\"Gil Shani Trio\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"venues\":[{\"id\":17,\"name\":\"The Horse Hospital\",\"address\":\"Colonnade\",\"city\":\"London\",\"country\":\"\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"promoters\":[{\"id\":136,\"name\":\"The Horse Hospital\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"stripe_account_id\":\"\",\"ticket_email\":\"\",\"custom_domain\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"ticket_tiers\":[{\"id\":732,\"name\":\"General Admission\",\"price\":10,\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"quantity_available\":100,\"quantity_sold\":5,\"resale_listed_count\":0,\"hidden\":false,\"password_protected\":false,\"is_pwyc\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"resale_enabled\":true,\"resale_when_event_sold_out\":false,\"sort_order\":0,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}]},{\"id\":648,\"name\":\"Repetitive Strain: Xanax + The Gall\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-21T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-22T01:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e4503bdf2f26f46436df72f7ac627072.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"REPETITIVE STRAIN EVENT:\\n\\nXANAX (LIVE – Penryn, Cornwall)\\n\\nLet's celebrate and vapourise: shredded electronic body music delivered in the most live and lithe sense, from minds behind GAMMA (Gob Nation) and FREAK GENES. \\n\\nTHE GALL (LIVE – Glasgow, Scotland)\\n\\nDeadly duo making London debut, pure rectangle music: metallic synth punk facilitated by new label SHUNNING GROUND. Members have been responsible for a huge amount of Scotland's finest digital detritus and wayward noise walls of the last decade including Unmaking, Time Binding Ensemble, Anxiety and Helena Celle's Mimetic Desire.\\n\\n+\\nREPETITIVE STRAIN DJs (Voices Radio)\\nThe most (un)wanted music, from MOTLASH \\u0026 VANITY CRYSTAL.\\n\\nat\\nSpanners, Brixton\\n20:00-01:00, 21.08.2026\\n£10.00, no-one turned away\\n18+, flat access, top bar\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"club\"},{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"gig\"}],\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"artists\":[{\"id\":1703,\"artist_name\":\"Xanax\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":1704,\"artist_name\":\"The Gall\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":1780,\"artist_name\":\"Repetitive Strain\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"venues\":[{\"id\":3,\"name\":\"Spanners\",\"address\":\"Arch 504, Ridgway Rd\",\"city\":\"London\",\"country\":\"U.K.\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"promoters\":[{\"id\":319,\"name\":\"Repetitive Strain\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"stripe_account_id\":\"\",\"ticket_email\":\"\",\"custom_domain\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"ticket_tiers\":[{\"id\":559,\"name\":\"Ticket\",\"price\":10,\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"quantity_available\":80,\"quantity_sold\":0,\"resale_listed_count\":0,\"hidden\":false,\"password_protected\":false,\"is_pwyc\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"resale_enabled\":true,\"resale_when_event_sold_out\":false,\"sort_order\":0,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"tags\":[{\"id\":12,\"name\":\"ebm\"},{\"id\":69,\"name\":\"punk\"},{\"id\":153,\"name\":\"cyberpunk\"},{\"id\":450,\"name\":\"synthpunk\"},{\"id\":451,\"name\":\"deathrock\"}]},{\"id\":802,\"name\":\"family affair volume X: a party for palestine\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-21T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-22T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"16ba86df652afd594b45d84a1db8d0b5.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Our last dance…. for now.\\n\\nFor our tenth edition, we’re welcoming two amazing artists to play for us, for the cause, for the very first time.\\n\\nAfter our sold out Palestine fundraiser party back in February, we return to the place where it all started for us: the small, sweaty loud basement of The Glove That Fits: a fitting place to hold the finale to our first run of parties.\\n\\nTickets have just gone live on RA - 100% of profits will be going to MSF UK as ever, raising urgent funds for medical aid in Gaza and beyond.\\n\\nTen parties in and over £10k raised - we’re going to take some time to take it all in, and go again on the other side.\\n\\nWe hope to see you there in a few weeks.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2493281\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"club\"}],\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"artists\":[{\"id\":42,\"artist_name\":\"Richard Gregory\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":840,\"artist_name\":\"Sheriff Boo\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2058,\"artist_name\":\"Séarlait\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"venues\":[{\"id\":222,\"name\":\"The Glove That Fits\",\"address\":\"\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"promoters\":[{\"id\":151,\"name\":\"Family Affair\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"stripe_account_id\":\"\",\"ticket_email\":\"\",\"custom_domain\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"tags\":[{\"id\":10,\"name\":\"techno\"},{\"id\":43,\"name\":\"progressive house\"},{\"id\":47,\"name\":\"minimal\"},{\"id\":48,\"name\":\"tech house\"}]},{\"id\":894,\"name\":\"Whole Danth Catalogue UK Edition\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-21T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-22T06:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"020a22a51c6fed82e245eb20051f9aa8.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"WHOLE DANTH CATALOGUE UK edition\\n~ Access to Contemporary Bass Music ~\\n\\nDoor £15\\n\\nActs:\\nOssia Live Set (Young Echo)\\nYOKEL (Plaque)\\nStranger\\nWoofoot (HHBush)\\nMore TBA\\n\\u0026 Secret Guest\\nSupported by:\\nHood by Foot\\n\\nA party rooted in leftfield bass music, drawing from the spirit of hip-hop and the attitude of punk.\\n\\nIn recent years, it has been influenced by Bristol’s culture and the wider European underground scene, exploring the intersection of dance music’s functionality and experimentation, where spatial abstraction meets physical groove.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2512304\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"club\"}],\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":833,\"name\":\"The Hot Snakes Night Club\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-22T10:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-13T16:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a384f9caaf459ae6f43b068640e6546d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The Hot Snakes Night Club is an immersive installation and  performance space by artist Chloe Langlois. Co-curated by TACO!  and Dinosaur Kilby, the club hosts a diverse programme of cabaret, live artist performance, workshops,  and experimental music from invited artists and guests.\\n\\nFor the duration of 4 weeks TACO! will be transformed into a multidisciplinary nightclub, complete with an artist-themed cocktail bar and an accompanying programme of cabaret, live performance and music. \\n\\nThe club launches on 22nd August with the event 24hr Gnosis - a 24 hr occult marathon of artist performances live-streamed on TACO!’s website and IRL in the gallery.     Artist contributors to the Hotsnakes Night Club include Chloe Langlois, Dinosaur Kilby, Kate Mahony, John Anthony Thadicaran,  Arianne Churchman,  Wayne Burrows, Qingqing Liu, Sister Punch, Friederike Steinert, OILS,  Frankie Roberts, Harun Morrison, Gusty Ferro, The Hundred CLub, Ugly Drugless,  Intimacy, The Electronic Audio Club, Mind Your Head Carbet, The Empty Void Orchestra, National Rails, Catherine Carter, R3YWYA, Kicho, Flying Carpets, Letti O’Burn \\u0026 Sunnyboy Tyson, Maryam Sandjari Hashemi, The Pipe Shoppe (Wojciech Rusin), Peter Groom, Sarah Doyle, Sparkes Thompson, The Receipt, and more….\\n\\nTACO!\\n2 Cygnet Square\\nLondon\\nSE2 9FA\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"club\"},{\"id\":3,\"name\":\"exhibition\"},{\"id\":7,\"name\":\"performance\"}],\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"promoters\":[{\"id\":390,\"name\":\"TACO!\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"stripe_account_id\":\"\",\"ticket_email\":\"\",\"custom_domain\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"tags\":[{\"id\":44,\"name\":\"art\"},{\"id\":128,\"name\":\"exhibition\"},{\"id\":218,\"name\":\"art exhibition\"},{\"id\":261,\"name\":\"experimental music\"},{\"id\":314,\"name\":\"installation\"},{\"id\":320,\"name\":\"art \\u0026 sound\"}]},{\"id\":834,\"name\":\"The Hot Snakes Night Club Presents: 24 hr Gnosis \",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-22T10:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-23T10:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"00b52ea97278b9c847043c17dd5bca53.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\\\"To inaugurate the Hotsnakes Night Club, please join us for 24hr Gnosis -  24hr’s of artist performances and live stream occult sleepover. Every hour for a whole day, Chloe Langlois has invited multiple artists to conjure and perform. Over the duration of 24hr hours, audiences can attend as a live studio audience, witnessing a range of participatory and passive performances. Access is free with a paid bar serving food and artist cocktails. \\n\\nAudiences wishing to take part in the gallery sleepover from  11pm til 9am can do so by booking. Places are limited. Please see the end of this web page for full details on how to take part in the sleepover.\\n\\n24hr Gnosis will be live-streamed on TACO!’s and the rtm websites.\\n\\nArtists participating in 24hr Gnosis include Chloe Langlois, John Anthony Thadicaran, Harun Morrison, Arianne Churchman, Kate Mahony, Wayne Burrows, Dinosaur Kilby, Qingqing Liu, Sister Punch, Friederike Steinert, OILS, Frankie Roberts, Dinosaur Kilby, Pil \\u0026 Galia Kollectiv, The Hundred Club,  and magical instruments from The Pipe Shoppe.\\\"\\n\\nTACO!\\n2 Cygnet Square\\nLondon\\nSE2 9FA\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"club\"},{\"id\":3,\"name\":\"exhibition\"},{\"id\":7,\"name\":\"performance\"}],\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"promoters\":[{\"id\":390,\"name\":\"TACO!\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"stripe_account_id\":\"\",\"ticket_email\":\"\",\"custom_domain\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"tags\":[{\"id\":128,\"name\":\"exhibition\"},{\"id\":145,\"name\":\"performance\"},{\"id\":218,\"name\":\"art exhibition\"},{\"id\":230,\"name\":\"experimental, left field, sound art, performance\"},{\"id\":231,\"name\":\"sound art\"},{\"id\":314,\"name\":\"installation\"},{\"id\":592,\"name\":\"sleepover\"}]},{\"id\":880,\"name\":\"BOHOMO PLACE - A Queer Community Day in Hackney Central\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-22T13:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-23T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a426bf6003899bdcbdc804c0c403eedb.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Hate gentrification, expensive hipster cafes, and big corporates and chains? Love Hackney, local venues and you’re a raging homo (or dyke/trans/non-binary/queer…)? \\n\\nThen BOHOMO PLACE is for you! \\n\\nOn Saturday 22 August, we’re taking over Bohemia Place in Hackney Central to offer an LGBTQIA+ Community Day alongside our friends Queertopia and Paper Dress Vintage.\\n\\nFrom 1pm till 3am! \\nAll the activities are FREE!\\nBar open from 1pm. Come have a drink! \\nThis event is part of our SOFT launch series, whilst we raise the funds that’ll allow us to be completely functional for our BIG OPENING (coming soon!). Check out our crowdfunder HERE.\\n\\nAnother way to support us is to just come down and have a drink (or several!) at the Joiners Heart from 1pm. \\n \\n\\nSCHEDULE:\\n\\nThe Joiners Heart (18, Bohemia Place)\\n\\n1-5pm: queer market + badge making workshop with Queertopia\\n\\n6-7.30pm: Drag King makeup workshop by Richard Energy  \\n\\n7.30-9pm: Think pub vibes, mingling \\u0026 chilling\\n\\n9-10pm: pop-up performances by Prinx Silver \\u0026 CYRO\\n\\n10pm-00.30am: DJ set by Trojan-Tyne (expect lots of gay bangers!)\\n\\n \\n\\nCheck out our A JOINERS HISTORY photo exhibition at the venue! Celebrating and remembering the legacy of the old Joiners Arms.\\n\\nAll our activities are free- please reserve your free ticket below so we know how many people to expect.\\n\\n \\n\\nPaper Dress Vintage (352a Mare Street)\\n\\n2-8pm: all dayer in back garden, by Queer Open Decks Collective (Expect from funk to disco, soul, hip hop, and house),\\n\\n10.30pm-3am: Disco Dyke Club Night\\n\\n \\n\\nACCESSIBILITY:\\n\\nThe Joiners Heart is step-free and wheelchair accessible via a ramp. \\n\\nWe have a wheelchair accessible toilet and two ambulant toilets. All toilets are all genders.\\n\\nWe have an accessible bar to order from.\\n\\nIf you have any questions or access needs, please send us a message through here or email: friendsjoinersarms@gmail.com\\n\\n \\n\\nTRANSPORT:\\n\\nYou can get here by Bus:\\n\\nHackney Central Station (Stop H, K, J): routes 253, 254, 106, 236, 394, N253.\\nMare Street (Stop T, E, F): routes 30, 38, 48, 55, 106, 236, 242, 253, 254, 276, 394, D6, N38, N55.\\nAmhurst Road (Stop L, R): routes 30, 56, 236, 253, 276\\n\\n\\nor by Overground:\\n\\nHackney Central, Mildmay Line, 5mins walk;\\nHackney Downs, Weaver Line, 10 mins walk\\nIt may be possible to park on Bohemia Place outside our unit, with some spaces available after 4.30pm.\\n\\n \\n\\nThis event is supported with funding from Hackney Council.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/38461/bohomo-place-a-queer-community-day-in-hackney-central\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"club\"},{\"id\":7,\"name\":\"performance\"},{\"id\":9,\"name\":\"workshop\"}],\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"venues\":[{\"id\":239,\"name\":\"The Joiners Heart\",\"address\":\"\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":240,\"name\":\"Paper Dress Vintage\",\"address\":\"\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"tags\":[{\"id\":62,\"name\":\"market\"},{\"id\":617,\"name\":\"drag king\"}]},{\"id\":884,\"name\":\"Handsworth Songs\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-22T14:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-22T17:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"beef0def17786822e926dba2565f52fc.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"An experimental documentary depicting protests around the UK, positioning the camera with the protesters rather than pointed at them.\\n\\n\\nHandsworth Songs (1986, 61 mins) is an experimental documentary depicting the lives of those in Handsworth, Brixton, and Tottenham during three different people’s uprisings in 1985, positioning the camera with the protesters rather than pointed at them.\\n\\nProduced by Black Audio Film Collective, Handsworth Songs interrogates the impact of colonialism and what it means to be Black-British at a time when these two terms were, and still are, at odds with each other.\\n\\nWhilst made for the television screen, Handsworth Songs has gone on to be screened in museums and art houses around the world. Following this screening we will hold a community conversation to mark the 15 year anniversary of Mark Duggan's death which caused uprisings across London and spread to other parts of England. We aim to consider how the riots of 1985 and 2011 are similar and different, understanding how they changed the course of history and also the way in which we, as an organisation in Haringey, interact with the history of the borough.\\n\\n\\n\\nThis is the third and final screening of HCC's Summer Programme: Making the Revolution Irresistible\\n\\nAbout the film \\u0026 filmmakers\\nTrailer\\n\\n\\nAWARDS:\\n\\nBritish Film Institute Grierson Award for Best Documentary in 1986.\\n\\nJOHN AKOMFRAH: Director\\n\\nFounder of Black Audio Film Collective, Akomfrah is a filmmaker who experiments with textures and sounds to create a landscape which explores the many outcomes of colonialism and immigration. Beginning with a career in television, via Chanel 4’s Workshop schemes, Akomfrah has more recently gone on to create installation pieces for art centres and museums internationally.\\n\\nOther works include:\\n\\nSeven Songs for Malcom X (1993)\\n\\nThe Stuart Hall Project (2013)\\n\\nThe Last Angel of History (1996)\\n\\n\\n\\nAbout our Guest Speaker\\n\\n\\nGuest Speaker: TBC\\n\\nBooking / Waiting List / Cancellation\\n\\n\\nPlease only book if you are confident you will be able to attend, as seating at this venue is limited. Due to safety regulations, walk-in entry cannot be guaranteed.\\n\\nThe registration form includes a small number of questions collected for reporting purposes. All data will be anonymised. Each attendee is required to complete the form. If you are booking on behalf of someone else and do not know an answer, please enter or select' N/A' where applicable.\\n\\nDue to the venue’s limited capacity, the event may sell out.If this happens, you can be added to the waiting list. When a ticket becomes available, you will receive an email to book it, and you will have 24 hours to complete your booking.\\n\\nIf you are unable to attend the event, please cancel your ticket(s) so that your place can be offered to someone else.\\n\\nWhy your donations are important?\\n\\nPlease read carefully! We’re introducing a Community Pricing to help cover the costs of our events. Choose the ticket tier that best reflects your current circumstances— considering income, housing, caring responsibilities, health, and day-to-day financial pressures. We trust you to choose what feels right. More on this system here.\\n\\nHCC is run by volunteers and does not receive any funding at the moment. Every donation you make will help us to support local venues and to organise other free screenings.\\n\\nIn a time of rising living costs and persistent barriers for marginalised communities in producing and accessing films that reflect their experiences and aspirations, we are committed to making our screenings free or pay-what-you-can.\\n\\nAbout the venue\\n\\nLordship Hub is a vibrant community centre and café at the heart of Lordship Rec, Tottenham’s largest park. The building is fully accessible, but located inside the park. If you need to be dropped off next to the building's main entrance (with the ramp), please contact us early so we can arrange the park's gate to be open. If you have any accessibility needs or questions, please contact us at haringeycommunitycinema@gmail.com.\\n\\nAbout HCC\\n\\nHaringey Community Cinema (HCC) was launched in April 2025 and is run by volunteers. Inspired by Brixton Community Cinema, HCC is aimed at bringing residents of Haringey together through film. Our mission is to showcase films that challenge, inspire, and spark critical reflection—films that make us think and act. Visit our website.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nCovid Policy\\n\\nHCC does not currently have an official COVID-19 policy. However, we remain mindful that many people are still vulnerable to the virus. We kindly ask attendees to take the following precautions to help keep our events safe and accessible for everyone:\\n\\nIf possible, please take a lateral flow test before attending.\\nIf you test positive or are experiencing any COVID-19 symptoms, please do not attend, even if you feel well.\\nWe welcome and encourage the use of masks inside the venue for those who wish to wear them.\\nPlease be considerate of others' comfort levels and respect requests for physical distance.\\nThank you for helping us create a safer and more inclusive space.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/handsworth-songs-registration-1995292310011\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":5,\"name\":\"film\"}],\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"venues\":[{\"id\":143,\"name\":\"Lordship Hub\",\"address\":\"Lordship Rec, Off Higham Road\",\"city\":\"London\",\"country\":\"\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"promoters\":[{\"id\":199,\"name\":\"Haringey Community Cinema\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"stripe_account_id\":\"\",\"ticket_email\":\"\",\"custom_domain\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"tags\":[{\"id\":22,\"name\":\"documentary\"},{\"id\":214,\"name\":\"Black British history\"},{\"id\":619,\"name\":\"Black Audio Film Collective\"}]},{\"id\":859,\"name\":\"ORMSIDE presents: DJ Marcelle (in Conversation \\u0026 Extended Set) with sinny \\u0026 Marylou\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-22T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-23T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"88aa80f506809834f61605f5e26e9a50.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"DJ Marcelle returns to Ormside on August 22nd. This time, marking her fourth annual visit to Ormside, we invite the notorious DJ and collector to join us for a live discussion in the space ahead of her extended club set. This offering presents the rare opportunity to hear Marcelle talk through her fascinating life and practice, guided by a handful of records from her colossal collection.\\n\\nFollowing the discussion, Marcelle’s customary 3 hour set is framed by sets from two masters of open-format selection: London-based Sinny and French-born Wheel of Fortune member Marylou.\\n\\nNow a household name in certain circles, DJ Marcelle’s work is evidence of a lifelong dedication to sonic detail. A champion of tracks that shouldn’t exist – hidden within the grooves of custom dubplates – her sets lead with curiosity, asserting a refreshing and open approach to dancefloor curation. As always, she must be seen to be believed.\\n\\nOn closing duties, Marylou returns to Ormside for the first time this year. A Morphine Records associate and member of b4b supergroup Wheel of Fortune (CCL, Nonogigsta, rRoxymore), her psychedelic and multi-faceted DJ sets have earned her position as a deeply respected DJ and organiser on the international stage.\\n\\nsinny opens the night, supporting DJ Marcelle for the 3rd time at Ormside since the yearly event first began. Weaving together strands of historically and personally resonant musics that trace and collapse timelines, sinny’s sets are tactile, thoughtful and narrative held together with textured and immersive sonics.\\n\\nLimited tickets available for pre-show talk (40)\\n\\nTalk - DJ Marcelle in Conversation 21:00 - 23:00\\n\\nClub - 23:00 - 05:00\\n\\nSupport from Carhartt WIP\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2480889\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"club\"},{\"id\":10,\"name\":\"talk\"}],\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"artists\":[{\"id\":8,\"artist_name\":\"Sinny\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":599,\"artist_name\":\"Marylou\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2216,\"artist_name\":\"DJ Marcelle\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"venues\":[{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"Ormside Projects\",\"address\":\"Penarth Centre, 32 Ormside Street\",\"city\":\"London\",\"country\":\"U.K.\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"promoters\":[{\"id\":53,\"name\":\"Ormside Projects\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"stripe_account_id\":\"\",\"ticket_email\":\"\",\"custom_domain\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"ticket_tiers\":[{\"id\":781,\"name\":\"3rd Release\",\"price\":17.35,\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"quantity_available\":20,\"quantity_sold\":0,\"resale_listed_count\":0,\"hidden\":false,\"password_protected\":false,\"is_pwyc\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"resale_enabled\":true,\"resale_when_event_sold_out\":true,\"sort_order\":0,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":782,\"name\":\"Talk \\u0026 Club Ticket\",\"price\":19.5,\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"quantity_available\":5,\"quantity_sold\":1,\"resale_listed_count\":0,\"hidden\":false,\"password_protected\":false,\"is_pwyc\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"resale_enabled\":true,\"resale_when_event_sold_out\":true,\"sort_order\":0,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}]},{\"id\":809,\"name\":\"Saltings EP launch gig\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-23T17:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-23T19:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"97e61a2c8364bd47dee950f45e6ce563.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join London-based folk duo Saltings for an intimate concert to mark the launch of their debut EP. \\n\\nSaltings blend delicate guitar and mandolin with rich harmonies reminiscent of Gillian Welch and Dave Rawlings. \\n\\nSupport from contemporary folk singer and multi-instrumentalist Pearl Fish, who is featured on the EP.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"gig\"}],\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"artists\":[{\"id\":2076,\"artist_name\":\"Saltings\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2077,\"artist_name\":\"Pearl Fish\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"venues\":[{\"id\":226,\"name\":\"Mascara Bar\",\"address\":\"72 Stamford Hill\",\"city\":\"\",\"country\":\"\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"promoters\":[{\"id\":380,\"name\":\"Saltings\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"stripe_account_id\":\"\",\"ticket_email\":\"\",\"custom_domain\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"ticket_tiers\":[{\"id\":698,\"name\":\"1st release\",\"price\":3,\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"quantity_available\":40,\"quantity_sold\":36,\"resale_listed_count\":0,\"hidden\":false,\"password_protected\":false,\"is_pwyc\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"resale_enabled\":true,\"resale_when_event_sold_out\":false,\"sort_order\":0,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":699,\"name\":\"2nd release\",\"price\":5,\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"quantity_available\":70,\"quantity_sold\":0,\"resale_listed_count\":0,\"hidden\":false,\"password_protected\":false,\"depends_on_tier_id\":698,\"dependency_sold_out\":false,\"is_pwyc\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"resale_enabled\":true,\"resale_when_event_sold_out\":false,\"sort_order\":0,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":702,\"name\":\"Pay what you can\",\"price\":0,\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"quantity_available\":30,\"quantity_sold\":2,\"resale_listed_count\":0,\"hidden\":false,\"password_protected\":false,\"is_pwyc\":true,\"is_free\":false,\"resale_enabled\":true,\"resale_when_event_sold_out\":false,\"sort_order\":3,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"tags\":[{\"id\":122,\"name\":\"folk\"},{\"id\":165,\"name\":\"live music\"},{\"id\":241,\"name\":\"contemporary folk\"}]},{\"id\":795,\"name\":\"Holding Company\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-30T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-23T19:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0feec9731c5afa30ca0f351adef78f74.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Dates: 31 July – 23 August\\nPublic opening event: Thursday 30 July, 6-9pm \\nGallery hours: Thursday – Friday, 1-7pm\\nAdditional viewings on the weekend are available by appointment. For more information and to book an appointment, please contact: aram@masharqa.com\\nAdmission: Free\\n\\nCurated by Aram Masharqa, the show probes the holding company as a fundamentally intangible corporate structure, bringing together new or unseen works and performances by H M Baker, José García Oliva, Luke Gould, Markéta Slaná, Maya King-Dabbs, Samra Mayanja, and Tawfik Naas.\\n\\nAbout the exhibition\\n\\nHolding Company is a group exhibition spanning object-based and event-based practices. Beginning from the place of neoliberal financial capitalism, the exhibition considers the affordances of ‘passive’ or ‘umbrella’ legal entities in the arts. While holding companies—corporate structures set up purely to hold assets and shield liability rather than produce goods—are everywhere in the contemporary art world, this show looks to the structure itself as a productive conceptual anchor.\\n\\nEmbracing rather than resisting the cultural rise of ‘corpcore’, the exhibition approaches this specific form of company on its own terms. If the gallery model is a kind of traditional company structure, perhaps the future of the gallery is holding companies all the way down: uber-streamlined, with staff and physical space abstracted out of the equation, and risk neatly packaged.\\n\\nAlongside the exhibition, ‘Holding Company’ features a public programme of three scheduled meetings, collectively titled ‘Out of Office (OOO)’, with talks between Aram Masharqa, Tawfik Naas, José García Oliva, and Samra Mayanja.\\n\\nAbout SET 91\\n\\nSET 91 is SET’s first in-house curated contemporary arts gallery, located in Old Street. Dedicated to supporting early-career contemporary artists, the gallery provides a non-profit platform for experimentation, collaboration, and the presentation of new work beyond commercial pressures.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":3,\"name\":\"exhibition\"},{\"id\":7,\"name\":\"performance\"},{\"id\":10,\"name\":\"talk\"}],\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"artists\":[{\"id\":1603,\"artist_name\":\"Samra Mayanja\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2025,\"artist_name\":\"Tawfik Naas\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2026,\"artist_name\":\"H M Baker\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2027,\"artist_name\":\"José García Oliva\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2028,\"artist_name\":\"Luke Gould\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2029,\"artist_name\":\"Markéta Slaná\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2030,\"artist_name\":\"Maya King-Dabbs\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"venues\":[{\"id\":86,\"name\":\"SET 91\",\"address\":\"91 Tabernacle Street\",\"city\":\"London\",\"country\":\"\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"promoters\":[{\"id\":130,\"name\":\"SET\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"stripe_account_id\":\"\",\"ticket_email\":\"\",\"custom_domain\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"tags\":[{\"id\":128,\"name\":\"exhibition\"},{\"id\":218,\"name\":\"art exhibition\"}]},{\"id\":693,\"name\":\"The Hotel presents... Agnese Toniutti plays the music of Philip Corner + Miles Lukoszevieze\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-24T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-24T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5f411260e63d6d364aa2d421a0fa94ad.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"In anticipation of the release of Philip Corner’s ‘Passage Through: A Ritual’ LP, The Hotel proudly  presents its first recital. \\n\\nThe Hotel invites Philip Corner’s pianist of choice, Agnese Toniutti, to Cafe OTO to perform a  concert of Corner’s works on the grand piano. \\n\\nAs prelude, The Hotel will host a premiere of Miles Lukoszevieze’s new piece ‘Self-Shadowing  Prey’ for live electronics and playback ensemble, inspired by the writings of Ghérasim Luca.\\n\\n\\n\\nPassage Through: A Ritual LP by Philip Corner is released 14th September, with advance copies available for sale at the event, alongside other titles from The Hotel.\\n\\nThis evening in The Hotel is curated by Philip Corner and Henry Cyer.\\n\\nMiles Lukoszevieze’s ‘Self-Shadowing Prey’ is commissioned by The Hotel, with the support of Hinrichsen Foundation.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.cafeoto.co.uk/events/the-hotel-presents-august-2026/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"gig\"},{\"id\":7,\"name\":\"performance\"},{\"id\":10,\"name\":\"talk\"}],\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"artists\":[{\"id\":1799,\"artist_name\":\"Agnese Toniutti\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":1800,\"artist_name\":\"Miles Lukoszevieze\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":1801,\"artist_name\":\"Philip Corner\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"venues\":[{\"id\":10,\"name\":\"Cafe Oto\",\"address\":\"18-22 Ashwin St\",\"city\":\"London\",\"country\":\"\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"promoters\":[{\"id\":148,\"name\":\"The Hotel\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"stripe_account_id\":\"\",\"ticket_email\":\"\",\"custom_domain\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"tags\":[{\"id\":246,\"name\":\"classical\"},{\"id\":483,\"name\":\"recital\"}]},{\"id\":889,\"name\":\"Everybody to Kenmure Street - Community Screening with Southwark and Lambeth Anti Raids\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-25T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-25T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"104a0792fcafc92cfc51e8b13d4dca64.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"In May 2021, a UK Home Office dawn raid triggers one of the most spontaneous and successful acts of civil resistance in recent memory. In Pollokshields, Scotland’s most diverse neighbourhood, hundreds of residents rush to the streets to stop the deportation of their neighbours. In today’s increasingly far-right political environment of immigration raids, deportation flights and border violence, Everybody to Kenmure Street is an empowering reminder of the importance of collective action.\\n\\n \\n\\nThe screening will be followed by a casual chat with Southwark and Lambeth Anti Raids @slantiraids on the organising they do in the area, and how you can get involved.\\n\\n \\n\\nAll are welcome, no matter your organising experience! The film is rated 12A.\\n\\n \\n\\nPay What You Can tickets are available from £1-8. This event is part of a series of community screenings around London with local anti raids groups, organised by april forrest lin 林森. All ticket revenue will be donated to Southwark and Lambeth Anti Raids after event costs have been covered.\\n\\n \\n\\n18:30 - Doors open\\n\\n19:00 - Film screening\\n\\n20:45 - Chat with Southwark and Lambeth Anti Raids\\n\\n21:00 - Chat ends, space stays open\\n\\n21:30 - Event ends\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/38273/everybody-to-kenmure-street-community-screening-with-southwark-and-lambeth-anti-raids\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":5,\"name\":\"film\"}],\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"venues\":[{\"id\":41,\"name\":\"SET Social\",\"address\":\"55a Nigel Road\",\"city\":\"London\",\"country\":\"United Kingdom\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"tags\":[{\"id\":155,\"name\":\"screening\"},{\"id\":195,\"name\":\"migrant rights\"},{\"id\":222,\"name\":\"community\"},{\"id\":623,\"name\":\"anti-raids\"},{\"id\":624,\"name\":\"collective action\"}]},{\"id\":863,\"name\":\"Phrasing: Poetry and DJs\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-25T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-25T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0f2d00c312f161c784832704aeb654c0.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"a lab of sonic curation and lyrical assembly.\\n\\npoets and disc jockeys perform in acoustic verse and electronic mix, in tandem and apart, held together in vibrational frequency by rhythm, by pause. \\n\\nsilence. suspension. drop. \\n\\nthe floor is open for poets who would like to experiment as part of the open jam. sign up on the night.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"club\"},{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"gig\"},{\"id\":7,\"name\":\"performance\"},{\"id\":8,\"name\":\"poetry\"}],\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"artists\":[{\"id\":531,\"artist_name\":\"Lana Baybie\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":674,\"artist_name\":\"Riwa Saab\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":935,\"artist_name\":\"Lottie\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":1529,\"artist_name\":\"CasuallyClued\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2226,\"artist_name\":\"Tice Cin\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"venues\":[{\"id\":138,\"name\":\"Studio 12\",\"address\":\"Studio 12, 1 Addington Square\",\"city\":\"London\",\"country\":\"\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"promoters\":[{\"id\":216,\"name\":\"Studio 12\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"stripe_account_id\":\"\",\"ticket_email\":\"\",\"custom_domain\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"ticket_tiers\":[{\"id\":775,\"name\":\"Pay What You Can\",\"price\":6,\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"quantity_available\":60,\"quantity_sold\":0,\"resale_listed_count\":0,\"hidden\":false,\"password_protected\":false,\"is_pwyc\":true,\"is_free\":false,\"resale_enabled\":true,\"resale_when_event_sold_out\":false,\"sort_order\":0,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":776,\"name\":\"General Admission\",\"price\":10,\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"quantity_available\":60,\"quantity_sold\":0,\"resale_listed_count\":0,\"hidden\":false,\"password_protected\":false,\"is_pwyc\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"resale_enabled\":true,\"resale_when_event_sold_out\":false,\"sort_order\":0,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"tags\":[{\"id\":211,\"name\":\"poetry\"},{\"id\":230,\"name\":\"experimental, left field, sound art, performance\"},{\"id\":261,\"name\":\"experimental music\"},{\"id\":415,\"name\":\"DJs\"},{\"id\":602,\"name\":\"electronic music\"},{\"id\":613,\"name\":\"rhythm\"}]},{\"id\":829,\"name\":\"Dub Sound Systems, Dhikr on Loudspeakers and the Politics of Amplification\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-27T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-27T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e7183acd7486366af611f6c8d17559ef.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Part screening, part listening session, part conversation, Dub Sound Systems, Dhikr on Loudspeakers and the Politics of Amplification is curated by Sarah El Miniawy in response to Joe Namy’s Cosmic Breath. \\n\\nThis event brings together artist GAIKA and artist-filmmaker Mahdy Abu Bahat in a conversation moderated by El Miniawy to trace the affinities between Moulid and Carnival through shared practices of amplification and temporary congregation.  \\n\\nMoulid endures as a counter-hegemonic practice, where Sufi transcendence becomes durational gathering and spectacle, sustained by the physical force of amplified sound. In these moments, dhikr, the act of remembrance in Islam, is felt differently by reciters, listeners and the urban landscape itself. Likewise, in London’s Carnival dub sound systems create an alternate environment within the city that gathers bodies around bass and volume, taking up space and amplifying communities that refuse to be erased.  \\n\\nRather than looking for a common genealogy, El Miniawy, GAIKA, and Abu Bahat will explore parallels across geographies when those on the margins temporarily occupy the centre through sound. Amplification and its technologies emerge as both sonic and social practice—from loudspeaker dhikr to dub bass—and the sound system as a temporary architecture for gathering. \\n\\nDoors open at 5.30pm; event starts at 6pm and ends at 8pm. \\n\\nImage credit: still from عـذر الوزة (The Goose's Excuse), 2023. A film by Mahdy Abo Bahat and Abdo Zin Eldin.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ibraaz.org/whats-on/dub-sound-systems-dhikr-on-loudspeakers-and-the-politics-of-amplification\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":9,\"name\":\"workshop\"},{\"id\":10,\"name\":\"talk\"}],\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"artists\":[{\"id\":2133,\"artist_name\":\"GAIKA\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2134,\"artist_name\":\"Mahdy Abu Bahat\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2135,\"artist_name\":\"Sarah El Miniawy\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"venues\":[{\"id\":118,\"name\":\"Ibraaz\",\"address\":\"93 Mortimer Street\",\"city\":\"London\",\"country\":\"\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"tags\":[{\"id\":4,\"name\":\"dub\"},{\"id\":6,\"name\":\"sound system\"},{\"id\":18,\"name\":\"bass\"},{\"id\":586,\"name\":\"dhikr\"},{\"id\":587,\"name\":\"amplification\"}]},{\"id\":881,\"name\":\"On Their Hearts They Walked - Gazan Photopoetry Book Event\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-27T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-27T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0826c5a4f751808001cd0e9e92da7c20.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us for an event presenting the collaboration photo poetry book ‘On Their Hearts They Walked’ by Gazan poet Jehad Jarbou and Gazan photographer Moayed Abu Ammouna. \\n\\nThe event will feature a presentation of and reading from the book, as well as music by Sara Masry and Paul on oud, Bint Mbareh, and a DJ set by Adan. The books will be available to purchase, as well as clothes by Shereen Abdelkareem and Amal Al Nakhala and limited Maqam Books selections. Food and drinks by Tigs Table. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":7,\"name\":\"performance\"},{\"id\":8,\"name\":\"poetry\"},{\"id\":10,\"name\":\"talk\"}],\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"artists\":[{\"id\":236,\"artist_name\":\"Bint Mbareh\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2279,\"artist_name\":\"Sara Masry\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"venues\":[{\"id\":75,\"name\":\"House of Annetta\",\"address\":\"25 Princelet Street\",\"city\":\"London\",\"country\":\"\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"promoters\":[{\"id\":211,\"name\":\"Against Apathy\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"stripe_account_id\":\"\",\"ticket_email\":\"\",\"custom_domain\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"ticket_tiers\":[{\"id\":788,\"name\":\"Low Income Ticket\",\"price\":5,\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"quantity_available\":15,\"quantity_sold\":1,\"resale_listed_count\":0,\"hidden\":false,\"password_protected\":false,\"is_pwyc\":true,\"min_price\":1,\"is_free\":false,\"resale_enabled\":true,\"resale_when_event_sold_out\":false,\"sort_order\":0,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":789,\"name\":\"Standard Ticket\",\"price\":10,\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"quantity_available\":35,\"quantity_sold\":2,\"resale_listed_count\":0,\"hidden\":false,\"password_protected\":false,\"is_pwyc\":true,\"min_price\":6,\"is_free\":false,\"resale_enabled\":true,\"resale_when_event_sold_out\":false,\"sort_order\":0,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":790,\"name\":\"Supporter Ticket \\u003c3\",\"price\":15,\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"quantity_available\":20,\"quantity_sold\":0,\"resale_listed_count\":0,\"hidden\":false,\"password_protected\":false,\"is_pwyc\":true,\"min_price\":11,\"is_free\":false,\"resale_enabled\":true,\"resale_when_event_sold_out\":false,\"sort_order\":0,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}]},{\"id\":867,\"name\":\"Ibrahim Alfa Jnr. \\u0026 feeo\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-27T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-27T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"bb5623d6a6a9d23b79385cc4eb6cb434.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\\nPresenting a double bill of vanguard techno producer Ibrahim Alfa Jnr. and vocalist and producer feeo at Ormside on Thursday 27th August. Ahead of carnival weekend celebrations and commemorations, we welcome two artists whose practices channel experiences of blackness via the collapsing and re-contextualisation of diasporic music idioms.\\n\\nWelcoming Ibrahim Alfa Jnr. to Ormside for his first UK show in a decade. A 90s veteran of UK techno, Alfa embodies resilience, having overcome serious health issues and systemic obstacles over the past few years. In response, his newest work ‘Infinite Black Inside’ (FO) tenderly serves fractured pulses and bass-heavy experiments, drawing on a full spectrum of radical Black music and a lifetime of experience. Free Jazz meets footwork, techno and dub – filtered through Alfa’s own lens to form a sonic imprint entirely his own, imbued with hope.\\n\\nfeeo is the solo project of London-based artist and vocalist Theodora Laird. Working across electronics, written word and performance – feeo investigates the feedback and tension between personal and political story. In her 2025 debut album ‘Goodness’ (AD93), feeo explores opposing forces of darkness and lightness, delivered via static hum, tape drones and whispers of dance music forms. On the 27th feeo presents a new solo performance at Ormside – her first London show since headlining ICA in February of this year.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"gig\"},{\"id\":3,\"name\":\"exhibition\"},{\"id\":5,\"name\":\"film\"}],\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"artists\":[{\"id\":1639,\"artist_name\":\"feeo\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2236,\"artist_name\":\"Ibrahim Alfa\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"venues\":[{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"Ormside Projects\",\"address\":\"Penarth Centre, 32 Ormside Street\",\"city\":\"London\",\"country\":\"U.K.\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"promoters\":[{\"id\":53,\"name\":\"Ormside Projects\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"stripe_account_id\":\"\",\"ticket_email\":\"\",\"custom_domain\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"ticket_tiers\":[{\"id\":777,\"name\":\"1st Release\",\"price\":13,\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"quantity_available\":15,\"quantity_sold\":0,\"resale_listed_count\":0,\"hidden\":false,\"password_protected\":false,\"is_pwyc\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"resale_enabled\":true,\"resale_when_event_sold_out\":true,\"sort_order\":0,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":778,\"name\":\"2nd release\",\"description\":\"\\nPresenting a double bill of vanguard techno producer Ibrahim Alfa Jnr. and vocalist and producer feeo at Ormside on Thursday 27th August. Ahead of carnival weekend celebrations and commemorations, we welcome two artists whose practices channel experiences of blackness via the collapsing and re-contextualisation of diasporic music idioms.\\n\\nWelcoming Ibrahim Alfa Jnr. to Ormside for his first UK show in a decade. A 90s veteran of UK techno, Alfa embodies resilience, having overcome serious health issues and systemic obstacles over the past few years. In response, his newest work ‘Infinite Black Inside’ (FO) tenderly serves fractured pulses and bass-heavy experiments, drawing on a full spectrum of radical Black music and a lifetime of experience. Free Jazz meets footwork, techno and dub – filtered through Alfa’s own lens to form a sonic imprint entirely his own, imbued with hope.\\n\\nfeeo is the solo project of London-based artist and vocalist Theodora Laird. Working across electronics, written word and performance – feeo investigates the feedback and tension between personal and political story. In her 2025 debut album ‘Goodness’ (AD93), feeo explores opposing forces of darkness and lightness, delivered via static hum, tape drones and whispers of dance music forms. On the 27th feeo presents a new solo performance at Ormside – her first London show since headlining ICA in February of this year.\",\"price\":15.2,\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"quantity_available\":15,\"quantity_sold\":0,\"resale_listed_count\":0,\"hidden\":false,\"password_protected\":false,\"depends_on_tier_id\":777,\"dependency_sold_out\":false,\"is_pwyc\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"resale_enabled\":true,\"resale_when_event_sold_out\":false,\"sort_order\":0,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"tags\":[{\"id\":8,\"name\":\"experimental\"}]},{\"id\":876,\"name\":\"Pre-launch • Ambient Sauna | Introspective Electronics x o.rbyss w/ Avsluta \\u0026 Luvandula\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-28T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-28T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4d7ccfc85b3b27a9a2a958b27c0fc560.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Pre-launch • Join us for the first weekend in our new venue, just two doors down from the original space you know and love! With the main launch party on Monday 31st, come down early for an exclusive preview and be the first to try out the new setup.\\n\\nIntrospective Electronics \\u0026 o.rbyss are our two longest-running monthly residencies, soundtracking Ambient Sauna since its very beginnings. For this special occasion, their founders, Avsluta and Luvandula, join forces for the first edition of the series in our new space, digging deep into their ambient and downtempo collections.\\n\\n*Book your 70-minute sauna session, arrive early and stay late for 4 hours of music in the lounge*\\n\\nABOUT AMBIENT SAUNA\\nOur silent Treehouse sauna and the chatty Herbal sauna are both equipped with a sound system for deep listening. Our Bunker sauna, the Tea Loft listening lounge and yard offer a social setting, perfect for a catch up and meeting new friends.\\n\\nABOUT SAUNA SOCIAL CLUB\\nThe Sauna Social Club is London's first dedicated sauna and ambient listening space. We blend saunas and ice baths with ambient music, making the perfect place to relax and recharge. We've grown out of a need for more healthy spaces to listen to great music. Our goal is to create a space that's designed for comfort and wellbeing that doesn't centre around consumption.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://tr.ee/Olqxg9oHjV\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":false,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"club\"},{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"gig\"}],\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"artists\":[{\"id\":127,\"artist_name\":\"luvandula\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":906,\"artist_name\":\"Avsluta\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"venues\":[{\"id\":31,\"name\":\"Sauna Social Club\",\"address\":\"Railway Arch 842 Brayards Road\",\"city\":\"London\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"promoters\":[{\"id\":132,\"name\":\"Sauna Social Club\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"stripe_account_id\":\"\",\"ticket_email\":\"\",\"custom_domain\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"tags\":[{\"id\":14,\"name\":\"ambient\"},{\"id\":42,\"name\":\"sauna\"},{\"id\":51,\"name\":\"downtempo\"},{\"id\":94,\"name\":\"listening\"},{\"id\":103,\"name\":\"music\"},{\"id\":415,\"name\":\"DJs\"},{\"id\":602,\"name\":\"electronic music\"}]},{\"id\":864,\"name\":\"Intimacy w/ Harry Smithson, Eleanor Arnold, Isabelle Pead and DJ Euro Kurd\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-28T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-28T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"74bee97cef6dc3aaff36d657448be280.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Intimacy, live at the Hot Snakes Night Club and on rtm.fm with an evening of experimental sound and performance art from friends and new faces. Existing as a monthly radio show on rtm since January 2024, Intimacy is a common ground for artists working with sound to test and develop new work through the live performance of radio.\\n\\nFREE\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":7,\"name\":\"performance\"}],\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"artists\":[{\"id\":2227,\"artist_name\":\"Harry Smithson\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2228,\"artist_name\":\"Eleanor Arnold\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2229,\"artist_name\":\"Isabelle Pead\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2230,\"artist_name\":\"DJ Euro Kurd\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"venues\":[{\"id\":233,\"name\":\"TACO!\",\"address\":\"2 Cygnet Square\",\"city\":\"London\",\"country\":\"United Kingdom\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"promoters\":[{\"id\":397,\"name\":\"Intimacy\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"stripe_account_id\":\"\",\"ticket_email\":\"\",\"custom_domain\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"tags\":[{\"id\":231,\"name\":\"sound art\"},{\"id\":261,\"name\":\"experimental music\"},{\"id\":309,\"name\":\"livestream\"},{\"id\":439,\"name\":\"performance art\"},{\"id\":521,\"name\":\"radio\"},{\"id\":614,\"name\":\"live broadcast\"}]},{\"id\":619,\"name\":\"Kiran Leonard / Jennifer Walton / Another Country $$$$\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-28T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-28T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"263f33e268a849f1c0f8aac0b64d3edb.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The Ivy House presents a night of live music, featuring three incredible artists a week before they each head to Dorset to perform at End of the Road Festival.\\n\\nKiran Leonard's unique and ambitious body of work spans more than a decade of frenetic noise rock, ornate avant-folk, DIY no-fi, and everything in between. Renowned for the range and intensity of his live performances, his current live group features members of caroline and Shovel Dance Collective.\\n\\nJennifer Walton is a London-based musician whose debut album Daughters explores grief, memory and surreal Americana. She’s also known for her work with Cryalot, Microplastics, Iceboy Violet, BABii, and remixes for Metronomy.\\n\\nAnother Country $$$$ are a Manchester-based audio-visual duo, born through the city’s experimental dance underbelly- combining shape-shifting electronic production, live drums and visuals. They craft blistering hybrid sets that fuse dub, jungle, DnB, garage, noise and hyperpop with a haunting cinematic edge.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"gig\"}],\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"artists\":[{\"id\":498,\"artist_name\":\"Jennifer Walton\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"